#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD2248-A expect=violation domain=TS
#note "Minted completeness sibling of FDA-SD2248 (Fix #239). Row 1 carries a COMPLETE ISO date and must NOT fire -- that is the negative control, and it is the row the parent's own valid scenario also passes. Row 2 is a partial (year-month) ISO date: valid ISO 8601, so the parent FDA-SD2248 stays silent on it, and this sibling is the ONLY rule that reports it. Row 3 is the same partial date under a different --PARMCD, which proves the parameter gate still selects."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 TSPARMCD=SENDTC TSVAL=2020-06
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 1 | SENDTC | Study End Date | 2020-01-15
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 2 | SENDTC | Study End Date | 2020-06
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 3 | DCUTDTC | Data Cutoff Date | 2020-06
